1
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:05,030
Thank you.
谢谢。

2
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:05,470
Iowa.
艾奥瓦州。

3
00:00:06,190 --> 00:00:07,450
I love you, Iowa.
艾奥瓦，我爱你们。

4
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:13,860
We have got a family up here of Republicans and Democrats and independents.
台上这个大家庭，有共和党人、民主党人，也有独立人士。

5
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:25,399
I want to first thank my wife, Christine, and our two boys, Tate and Axel.
首先，我要感谢妻子克里斯汀，以及我们的两个儿子泰特和阿克塞尔。

6
00:00:25,399 --> 00:00:25,620
For your support and for the sacrifices that you shared in our effort.
感谢你们的支持，以及为了我们的共同努力而作出的牺牲。

7
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,320
I couldn't have done it without you.
没有你们，我做不到这一切。

8
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:27,790
Truly.
真的。

9
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:36,296
Christine, you've carried [inaudible].
克里斯汀，你承担了……[此处听不清]。

10
00:00:36,296 --> 00:00:36,446
You've offered helpful advice.
你给了我许多有益的建议。

11
00:00:36,446 --> 00:00:36,596
You deserve just as much credit for this as I do.
这份功劳，你和我一样值得拥有。

12
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:47,373
My parents, my parents, Leslie and Kevin, my sister Jen, my in-laws.
我的父母莱斯利和凯文，我的姐姐珍，以及我的岳父母。

13
00:00:47,373 --> 00:00:47,800
Nix.
尼克斯。

14
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,236
Your help was invaluable in deciding which tie to wear for the third debate.
你在帮我决定第三场辩论该戴哪条领带这件事上，帮了大忙。

15
00:00:50,236 --> 00:00:50,386
Thank you for that.
谢谢你。

16
00:00:50,386 --> 00:00:55,849
Really appreciate that, Augie.
真的很感谢你，奥吉。

17
00:00:55,849 --> 00:00:59,652
Thank you for being my [inaudible].
谢谢你做我的……[此处听不清]。

18
00:00:59,652 --> 00:01:04,335
And most importantly, Walter, rest in peace.
还有最重要的，沃尔特，愿你安息。

19
00:01:04,335 --> 00:01:06,410
The energy and the excitement that he brought to the campaign was irreplaceable.
他为这场竞选带来的活力与激情，无可替代。

20
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:12,419
Christine said something profound the other day.
克里斯汀前几天说了一句很深刻的话。

21
00:01:12,419 --> 00:01:25,163
She had been bracing for a difficult October, and yet everything that we imagined it would be was nothing compared to how hard it has been losing Walter.
她原本已准备好面对艰难的十月，但我们想象中的一切困难，都远远比不上失去沃尔特的痛苦。

22
00:01:25,163 --> 00:01:25,470
There are countless other family members and friends who have been with me every step of the way.
还有无数亲朋好友，在每一步都陪伴着我。

23
00:01:26,190 --> 00:01:32,137
It has been a long 18 months on the campaign trail, and I could not have gotten here without your support.
竞选路上的这十八个月很漫长；没有你们的支持，我走不到这里。

24
00:01:32,137 --> 00:01:38,892
You know who you are.
你们知道我说的是谁。

25
00:01:38,892 --> 00:02:03,057
Thank you to my running mate and Iowa's next lieutenant governor, Dave Muhlbauer.
感谢我的竞选搭档，艾奥瓦下一任副州长，戴夫·米尔鲍尔。

26
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:05,270
We love Dave, don't we?
我们爱戴夫，对不对？

27
00:02:06,610 --> 00:02:07,310
Love this guy.
我喜欢这个人。

28
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:12,570
When I asked him to join the ticket, we were actually at his mom's house with his mom.
当我邀请他加入竞选搭档时，我们其实正和他的母亲一起，在她家里。

29
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:24,379
I looked around the house and I could tell that he had the same kind of upbringing that I did.
我环顾那间房子，就知道他的成长环境和我很像。

30
00:02:24,379 --> 00:02:26,472
Raised by good people with good values.
都是由善良、拥有良好价值观的人抚养长大。

31
00:02:26,472 --> 00:02:29,890
Same kinds of sayings on the wall, same kinds of decoration.
墙上挂着相似的箴言，家里有着相似的装饰。

32
00:02:29,890 --> 00:02:39,279
And I have got to say, anyone who can get elected in a county that goes 75 percent for the other party in the race for president has to be a peacemaker
我得说，一个人在总统选举中有百分之七十五选民支持另一党的县里，还能胜选，他一定是一个善于促成和解的人，

33
00:02:39,279 --> 00:02:40,453
And a public servant.
一个真正的公仆。

34
00:02:40,453 --> 00:02:44,424
Amen for that.
为此说一声“阿门”。

35
00:02:44,424 --> 00:02:44,574
Literally.
我是认真的。

36
00:02:44,574 --> 00:02:54,234
No wonder why we had multiple Republican elected officials who endorsed me just because I picked Dave.
难怪好几位共和党民选官员，仅仅因为我选择了戴夫，就支持了我。

37
00:02:54,234 --> 00:02:54,798
I had not talked to them.
我没有跟他们谈过。

38
00:02:54,798 --> 00:02:55,268
I had not called them.
没有给他们打过电话。

39
00:02:55,268 --> 00:02:56,500
I had not asked for their endorsement.
也没有要求他们背书。

40
00:02:56,500 --> 00:03:04,777
They just saw that I picked Dave Muhlbauer, and they were like, well, me too, then.
他们只是看到我选了戴夫·米尔鲍尔，就说：“那我也支持。”

41
00:03:04,777 --> 00:03:04,927
Yeah.
是啊。

42
00:03:04,927 --> 00:03:08,748
So we got a good one here.
所以，我们找到了一位好搭档。

43
00:03:08,748 --> 00:03:11,167
Iowa, a really good one.
艾奥瓦，是一位非常好的搭档。

44
00:03:11,167 --> 00:03:11,317
He brings along a great family, too.
他还带来了一个很棒的家庭。

45
00:03:11,317 --> 00:03:17,116
Thank you to Linda as well and the kids for letting Dave help me get here today.
也感谢琳达和孩子们，让戴夫能够帮助我走到今天。

46
00:03:17,116 --> 00:03:27,000
Very excited for our partnership ahead and to have his work ethic especially added to serve Iowans.
我非常期待今后的合作，尤其期待以他勤恳的工作精神，一起服务艾奥瓦人民。

47
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,280
To Republican and independent public endorsers of this campaign: for your courage and for your leadership.
感谢那些公开支持这场竞选的共和党人和独立人士，感谢你们的勇气和领导力。

48
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:28,880
Genuinely.
发自内心地感谢。

49
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:46,350
We do live in a broken, two-choice political system where it requires real listening to learn that a candidate who is in the other party does not see you as the enemy.
我们确实生活在一个失灵的、只有两种党派选择的政治体系中；只有认真倾听，才能明白另一党的候选人并没有把你视作敌人。

50
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:46,500
You listened.
你们选择了倾听。

51
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:53,412
You knew that you would receive some negative reaction for endorsing across party lines.
你们知道，跨党派支持会招来一些负面反应。

52
00:03:53,412 --> 00:04:08,122
But you knew that the angriest ones are the loudest, and you knew that you were willing to stand publicly on principle to support returning our state to balanced government.
但你们也知道，最愤怒的人往往声音最大；你们仍愿意公开坚持原则，支持让这个州重新拥有相互制衡的政府。

53
00:04:08,122 --> 00:04:14,103
We have to have bigger hearts and minds than just our party.
我们的胸襟与视野，必须超越自己的党派。

54
00:04:14,103 --> 00:04:19,686
And everyone who did that across party lines with a public endorsement showed that.
每一个跨越党派、公开表达支持的人，都证明了这一点。

55
00:04:19,686 --> 00:04:25,468
And we thank you for it.
我们为此感谢你们。

56
00:04:25,468 --> 00:04:36,069
To Iowa Democrats: you have had a hard few years here in Iowa.
艾奥瓦的民主党人，过去几年，你们过得很艰难。

57
00:04:36,069 --> 00:04:46,457
But balanced government has been restored.
但现在，相互制衡的政府恢复了。

58
00:04:46,457 --> 00:04:47,190
You stayed strong.
你们坚持住了。

59
00:04:47,590 --> 00:04:48,190
You worked hard.
你们付出了努力。

60
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:53,610
So many of you feel what I feel about the divisiveness of our political system.
很多人和我一样，感受到我们政治体制中的严重分裂。

61
00:04:53,610 --> 00:05:06,740
And you were excited to have somebody as a candidate in your party who was actually talking about that and focusing on it.
当自己党内终于有一位候选人认真谈论、关注这个问题时，你们感到振奋。

62
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:17,443
But even among those of you who do not like that part as much, well, the vast majority of you understood that the smallest party has to appeal to reasonable-minded people in
即使有些人不那么认同这部分主张，绝大多数人仍明白：一个规模最小的政党，必须争取其他党派中愿意理性思考的人，

63
00:05:17,443 --> 00:05:24,678
Other parties if it wants to build a coalition that reaches a majority.
才能建立获得多数支持的联盟。

64
00:05:24,678 --> 00:05:34,138
Because of all of us coming together, in January no Iowan has to fear their government anymore.
因为大家团结起来，到一月，任何艾奥瓦人都不必再害怕自己的政府。

65
00:05:34,138 --> 00:05:37,898
To those who did not vote for me, I am going to listen to you and serve you just the same.
对于没有投票给我的人，我同样会倾听你们、为你们服务。

66
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:52,652
I hope you already know that I had senior leaders in the auditor's office who were an independent and a Republican who had made campaign contributions to my opponent in 2018.
希望你们知道：在审计长办公室，我曾任用一位独立人士，以及一位在二〇一八年向我的对手捐过竞选款的共和党人担任高级领导。

67
00:05:52,652 --> 00:05:53,744
I am going to continue a similar approach.
我会继续采取类似的做法。

68
00:05:53,744 --> 00:05:59,538
I hope, if you see me out and about in our state — I mean, I am going to be out and about,
如果你们在州内各处遇到我——我确实会常常到各地去，

69
00:05:59,538 --> 00:06:01,548
And I know that there are plenty of Iowans who did not vote for me.
我知道，有很多艾奥瓦人没有投票给我。

70
00:06:01,548 --> 00:06:01,698
So you are going to see me out and about.
所以，你们会在各地见到我。

71
00:06:01,698 --> 00:06:01,848
I hope that you stop me.
我希望你们叫住我。

72
00:06:01,848 --> 00:06:13,199
I hope you introduce yourself, and I hope you kindly tell me why you did not vote for me.
希望你们介绍自己，也希望你们友善地告诉我，为什么没有投票给我。

73
00:06:13,199 --> 00:06:20,338
I hope you also keep an open mind, because you are going to get to know me better over the next four years,
也希望你们保持开放的心态，因为接下来四年，你们会更加了解我，

74
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:23,132
And maybe you will feel differently the next time.
也许下一次，你们就会有不同的看法。

75
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:28,671
Bottom line is this: again, for the folks who did not vote for me, I am going to work just as hard for you as I do for anyone else.
归根结底，对于没有投票给我的人，我会和为其他任何人一样，全力为你们工作。

76
00:06:28,690 --> 00:06:36,856
Thank you also for voting and for being a part.
也感谢你们投票，感谢你们参与其中。

77
00:06:36,856 --> 00:06:37,006
Appreciate that.
谢谢你们。

78
00:06:37,006 --> 00:06:42,670
Now, given that we are here tonight, Democrats and independents and Republicans together, as we did at 200 town halls and countless rallies across this state,
今晚，民主党人、独立人士和共和党人齐聚这里，就像我们在全州两百场市民大会和无数集会中那样，

79
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:53,327
Who is going to start us in singing America the Beautiful?
谁来带领我们唱《美丽的阿美利加》？

80
00:06:53,327 --> 00:06:53,477
You know what?
你们知道吗？

81
00:06:53,477 --> 00:06:53,627
Hold on.
等一下。

82
00:06:53,627 --> 00:06:56,011
We did not have anybody go yet, right?
还没有人开始，对吧？

83
00:06:56,011 --> 00:06:58,134
All right, I am going to step aside.
好，我先让到一旁。

84
00:06:58,134 --> 00:07:11,351
And just so that we have a clear note and one person who we can all join in,
为了有一个清楚的起音，让大家能跟着一个人一起唱，

85
00:07:11,351 --> 00:07:14,760
Virginia will start us off.
就请弗吉尼娅带我们开头。